  "stemBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Expand and simplify (x − 3)(x + 6)."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Think first: The signs are mixed, so the constant will be negative and the middle term takes the sign of the larger number."
    },
    {
      "type": "asset",
      "storagePath": "assets/question_visuals/p053_q04.jpg",
      "altText": "Source visual for edmar-csec-p053-q04 from workbook page 53."
    }
  ],
  "solutionSteps": [
    {
      "stepNo": 1,
      "instruction": "Multiply the first terms.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "x × x"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: x²"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 2,
      "instruction": "Multiply the outer and inner pairs.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "x × 6 = 6x and (−3) × x = −3x"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: 6x − 3x"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 3,
      "instruction": "Multiply the last terms.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "(−3) × 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: −18"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 4,
      "instruction": "Collect the middle terms.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "6x − 3x = 3x"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: x² + 3x − 18"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "strategyBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Expand each pair of terms, then combine the two x-terms."
    }
  ],
  "finalAnswerBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "x² + 3x − 18"
    }
  ],
  "whyThisWorks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "The coefficient of x is −3 + 6 = 3 and the constant is (−3) × 6 = −18, both consequences of multiplying out every pair. Because 6 is larger in size than 3, the middle term ends up positive even though one bracket subtracts. Knowing that the sign of the middle term follows the numerically larger value is a quick way to sense-check mixed-sign expansions."
    }
  ],
